{"id": "meta_modelers_guide.composites.cellcell-compete-mm", "name": "cellcell-compete-mm", "description": "Cell-cell (colony) interface-substitutability twin of cellcell-compete: BYTE-IDENTICAL CpmColonyField ports and the same 60x60 shared glucose field, but each cell's INTERNAL per-cell metabolism is swapped from constraint-based dynamic-FBA (e_coli_core, O2-capped) to a lumped Michaelis-Menten / Monod metabolism (mechanism='mm', no cobra). Each competitor keeps its OWN saturating glucose uptake v = glucose_vmax*glc/(glucose_km+glc) -- so the vmax 10-vs-4 asymmetry that drives competitive exclusion is preserved by construction -- then realizes growth by a fixed biomass yield (mm_yield*v) and acetate overflow (mm_overflow*v standing in for the dFBA O2-cap mixed-acid overflow). The mm_* params are TUNED so the colony interface-level observables (per-cell + total biomass, the competition ratio, total CPM volume, field glucose depletion + acetate plume) track the dFBA cellcell-compete within ~6%. This lifts the flagship single-cell dFBA<->MM substitutability up to the multi-cell colony composition level: same colony<->field interface, a different (cobra-free) box behind every cell.", "parameters": {}, "state": {"fields": {"glucose": [[3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0], [3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0], [3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.0, 3.